# text_id = 1934
# text = Now the Minister for Labour said at Nottingham that in order to clear away any misconception arising from statements made by himself , Mr. Henderson , and Mr. Neville Chamberlain , he wanted it to be distinctly understood , regarding remuneration , that if a man volunteering for national work had been receiving 40s . a week in Nottingham , he would be paid as much if taken to Newcastle .
