# text_id = 1938
# text = Then wages can only follow prices if there is an exceptional demand for labour — that is to say , if you are now making guns or khaki or boots for the Army or Navy , inasmuch as there is now exceptional demand for their labour , they can , of course , find the law of supply and demand being tilted in their direction and they can get more wages .
