# text_id = 1958
# text = And as in the hospitals so in the concentration camps the English soldiers , if what they state is correct , were habitually worse fed ; they were left in a disgusting state of filth ; they were denied the small privileges which were accorded to their fellow - prisoners , and if there was any particularly repulsive work to perform they were always the men selected to do it .
