# text_id = 1977
# text = Then , when we ask the Board of Trade to do a simple thing for the manufacturers — that is , to see that the price of coal is not raised extortionately — the right hon . Gentleman says he cannot do it , not so much because of the sanctity of contracts , as because it would occupy too much of the time of the officials of the Board .
