# text = This Amendment proposes that in future , so long as the aggrieved member shall allege that he has been deprived of those benefits for political purposes , for political reasons , or on political grounds , that he can go in the face of that Fourth Section of the Act of 1871 — can go to the Registrar and the Registrar can make any order he likes without limit or stint .
