# text = But , in spite of that , the Egyptian Government went on under the native Ministry , with civilian advisers , exactly as if martial law had not existed , and they did not intrude except in cases where it was absolutely necessary , and the administration under successive generals , particularly General Maxwell and General Allen by was a striking proof that generals are not always pure militarists .
